WEBVTT

1
00:00:06.380 --> 00:00:09.500
In addition to keeping redundant backups of information,

2
00:00:09.630 --> 00:00:13.699
you also have a redundant source of power to provide backup power.

3
00:00:13.710 --> 00:00:17.420
So you have an uninterrupted power supply or UPS

4
00:00:17.809 --> 00:00:21.600
transfer switches or transformers may also be involved and in

5
00:00:21.610 --> 00:00:24.729
case the power is interrupted by weather or blackouts,

6
00:00:24.739 --> 00:00:27.159
a backup generator is essential.

7
00:00:27.389 --> 00:00:31.684
Often there will be two generators connected by two different transfer switches.

8
00:00:31.995 --> 00:00:35.775
These generators might be powered by diesel or gasoline or

9
00:00:35.784 --> 00:00:39.814
other fuel such as propane or even by solar panels,

10
00:00:39.825 --> 00:00:43.284
a hospital or essential government agency might contract with more

11
00:00:43.294 --> 00:00:46.115
than one power company and be on two different grids.

12
00:00:46.125 --> 00:00:47.494
In case one goes out,

13
00:00:47.674 --> 00:00:50.014
this is what we mean by redundancy.